> That is exactly _not_ what that page says.
> Yes, the staff Hermes carries is the caduceus, which is a winged staff
> with snakes. However, this is a herald's staff (and originally seems to
> have been a magical staff) - which makes sense, since Hermes is the
> messenger of the gods.
> However, this Hermetic staff has nothing to do with the medical staff at
> all, though it's often confused with it. The Aesculape, which is the
> medical staff, is an ordinary staff with a _single_ snake wound around
> it and no wings whatsoever.
